Z||000000||CanadianGT||05-22-2001||04:17 PM||||So I gt home From school today, and turn on the TV.  Motoring 2001 is on, and normally I dont watch it, but I decided to today. As I was watching it I was thinking to myself how I wished they would show something on the Fiero.  Well not 5 minutes into the show, What do I see, but a Fiero GT.  The show is tagging along in OPP Police Cruisers, and they are out trying to catch speeders and people who talk  on cell Phones.  The 2nd person they pulled over  blew past the cop in there fastback GT.  They then proceeded to make 2 lane changes without signaling.  The cop pulled the lady over and they showed him giving her a ticket.  He then noticed she was driving with a suspended license, and showed the car being loaded onto a tow truck and being towed away.  On the Front of the Fiero at the Top of the windshield was RSM motorports in huge letters(Make the supercharger for the Fiero). The car had really nice rims too. I wonder if this was anyone on the form???||||reg||1
Z||000001||Neverfinished||05-22-2001||05:50 PM||||I noticed that too... too bad it got towed, poor car. Looked like a nice blond drivin  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>To Be Old And Wise, You First Must Be Young And Stupid.-----------------<BR>It's not a waste of time... If you are wasted at the time||||reg||1
Z||000002||kslish||05-23-2001||12:41 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by CanadianGT:<BR><B>Motoring 2001 is on, and normally I dont watch it, but I decided to today. As I was watching it I was thinking to myself how I wished they would show something on the Fiero.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That Canadian television program did a special on the Fiero (and on the Fiero Shop up there in Canada) a year or two ago...I think it was in 1999.  They devoted about 15 minutes to it.  Pretty cool, they showed 3.8 conversions and had interviews with some owners and stuff.  I have it on video tape someplace but I don't play it much anymore since the tape is getting a little worn (I showed it to a lot of people).  I hope to digitize it and save it to a VideoCD if I ever get around it.<P>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> <P>||||reg||1
